          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "EXERCISE 2.2"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.168,
            0.898,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find the zeroes of the following quadratic polynomials and verify the relationship between the zeroes and the coefficients. (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 2 }   -   2 x   -   8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 s ^ { 2 }   -   4 s   +   1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 x ^ { 2 } - 3 - 7 x"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 u ^ { 2 }   + 8 u"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (v) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t ^ { 2 }   -   1 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (vi) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 x ^ { 2 }   -   x   -   4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.256,
            0.898,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find a quadratic polynomial each with the given numbers as the sum and product of its zeroes respectively. 4 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } , - 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "- \\frac { 1 } { 4 } , \\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\sqrt { 2 } } , { \\frac { 1 } { 3 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "_ { 0 , \\sqrt { 5 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.391,
            0.251,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.4 Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.418,
            0.575,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this chapter, you have studied the following points:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.441,
            0.899,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Polynomials of degrees 1, 2 and 3 are called linear, quadratic and cubic polynomials respectively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.482,
            0.9,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A quadratic polynomial in x with real coefficients is of the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax^{2} + bx + c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " where a, b, c are real numbers with "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a   \\neq   0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.523,
            0.9,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The zeroes of a polynomial "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p ( x )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are precisely the x-coordinates of the points, where the graph of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y   =   p ( x )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " intersects the x - axis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.564,
            0.9,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A quadratic polynomial can have at most 2 zeroes and a cubic polynomial can have at most 3 zeroes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.604,
            0.765,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. If   and   are the zeroes of the quadratic polynomial "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a x ^ { 2 } + b x + c ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.636,
            0.418,
            0.674
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\alpha + \\beta = - \\frac{b}{a}, \\quad \\alpha \\beta = \\frac{c}{a}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.683,
            0.764,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. If α, β, γ are the zeroes of the cubic polynomial "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax^{3} + bx^{2} + cx + d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.715,
            0.405,
            0.751
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\frac { - b } { a }"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.773,
            0.432,
            0.805
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "\\alpha \\beta + \\beta \\gamma + \\gamma \\alpha = \\frac { c } { a } ,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.824,
            0.366,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\alpha \\beta \\gamma = { \\frac { - d } { a } }   ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
